I've been following the discussion here about the role of randomly generated
WoW's. I just decided they should definitely be outlawed or wishes should
be seriously weakened: I was playing a Tourist, and find a WoW with three
charges on level five or so, and hey presto, +3 rustproof Mjollnir, ditto
GDSM, ditto ditto GoP, ditto ditto ditto CoP. What then? Yawn! It was so
boring that when I ran into a nice-looking succubus I said yes to everything
she suggested and got clobbered by a jealous flesh golem. Highly appropriate.

Early WoW's take all the fun out of hacking. (Oh yeah, I found a magic lamp,
too.) Magic lamps are another kettle of fish: one wish spices up a game 
nicely (on occasion), but three or four is too much. Take note, dev team!

(And don't tell me not to use the wishes if I don't want 'em -- I always
was a sucker for temptation. As seen with the above succubus episode.)

